# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Runtime state: fragment store, statistics database, and their WAL sidecars.
# `data/` is the default when no configuration says otherwise, so it appears the
# first time anyone runs the binary.
/data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Local configuration, which usually carries an upstream key
/kompressor.toml
/config.toml
*.local.toml
.env
.env.*

# Benchmark output: recorded runs and corpora are regenerated, not committed.
# The corpus and baseline that the tests need are under fixtures/ and are
# deliberately not ignored.
#
# `runs/` is where `scripts/harbor/suite.sh` writes by default
# (`KOMPRESSOR_RUNS`, falling back to `$ROOT/runs`). The codex sweep and
# `scripts/smoke.sh` write outside the checkout entirely — `$HOME/.cache` and
# `mktemp -d` — so neither needs a rule here.
# Unanchored: a run directory is also written wherever KOMPRESSOR_RUNS points,
# which is often a sibling of the repo checkout rather than its root.
runs/
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
!fixtures/*.jsonl
!fixtures/*.jsonl.gz

# Python tooling. `scripts/` is a package-less pile of executables, so importing
# one (which the benchmark tooling does) leaves a __pycache__ beside it holding
# .pyc files named after whatever the script was called at the time — stale and
# misleading the moment anything is renamed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The thin clients under clients/. Their build output and installed
# dependencies are regenerated by `npm install`, `npm run build` and
# `python -m build`; the sources, package.json and pyproject.toml are committed.
# package-lock.json is deliberately not ignored: commit it if one is created.
/clients/typescript/node_modules/
/clients/typescript/dist/
/clients/typescript/*.tsbuildinfo
/clients/python/build/
/clients/python/dist/

# Cursor hook mode, installed into a checkout. `kompressor hook install cursor
# --project` writes hooks.json and mcp.json into the workspace's .cursor/, and
# a test of the allow-list writes cli.json there; all three name this machine's
# binary, configuration and home directory by absolute path, so they are local
# by construction. The workspace can be any directory below the root, hence
# `**/`. Not the whole of .cursor/ — rules and other files a team shares
# belong there too.
**/.cursor/hooks.json
**/.cursor/mcp.json
**/.cursor/cli.json

# Claude Code: personal permissions, and the worktrees it creates for isolated
# sessions — each a full checkout of this repository.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Agent tooling state. Serena writes a per-project symbol cache and config here
# the first time it activates on the repo; its own .gitignore covers only
# `cache/` and `project.local.yml`, so `project.yml` would otherwise be
# committed. Nothing in it is needed to build or test — deleting it just makes
# Serena re-index.
.serena/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Review output, not part of the project
findings.md

# Local experiments and working notes. The Claude Desktop experiment kit and
# the dated investigation write-ups under docs/investigations/ reference local
# run directories and are not part of the published documentation; nothing
# committed links to either.
scripts/claude-desktop-experiment/
docs/investigations/
docs/research/
